WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
Cranberry Lime Snowball Cookies. 33 min · 24 servings · American

2
00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:08.000
Ingredients: 9. 1 cup unsalted butter, softened; 1/2 cup powdered sugar; 1 teaspoon vanilla extract; 2 cups all-purpose flour

3
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:12.000
Step 1. Preheat oven to 350°F (175°C).

4
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:16.000
Step 2. In a large bowl, cream together the softened butter and 1/2 cup powdered sugar until light and fluffy.

5
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:20.000
Step 3. Stir in vanilla extract, flour, and salt until combined.

6
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:24.000
Step 4. Fold in chopped cranberries, lime zest, and lime juice until evenly distributed.

7
00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:28.000
Step 5. Roll dough into 1-inch balls and place on an ungreased baking sheet, spacing about 1 inch apart.

8
00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:32.000
Step 6. Bake for 15–18 minutes or until the bottoms are lightly golden.

9
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:36.000
Step 7. Let the cookies cool for a few minutes, then roll them in the remaining 1 cup of powdered sugar while still warm.

10
00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:40.000
Step 8. Once completely cool, roll them in the powdered sugar again for a second coating.

11
00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:43.000
You're ready. Use Make It for checkboxes on the page.
